{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "01a08154-4c27-7551-9cfa-e8e7d2bcf73a", "turn_id": "01a159c7-08da-7da0-beba-8f34917dec3f", "item_id": "call_9f1ae0bb904147ec985c9ba268110a49", "rollout_ordinal": 4546, "created_at_ms": 1792507590400, "item_type": "webSearch", "updated_at_ordinal": 4546, "started_at_ms": 1792507590400, "completed_at_ms": 1792507592500}, "item": {"type": "webSearch", "id": "call_9f1ae0bb904147ec985c9ba268110a49", "query": "site.huggingface.co Qwen3 0.6B model card languages thinking ...", "action": {"type": "search", "query": null, "queries": ["site.huggingface.co Qwen3 0.6B model card languages thinking", "site.huggingface.co HuggingFaceTB SmolLM2 360M Instruct model card language"]}, "results": [{"type": "text_result", "domain": "github.com", "ref_id": "turn22search0", "snippet": "SmolLM2 is a family of compact language models available in three size: 135M, 360M, and 1.7B parameters. ... You can find more details on how", "title": "smollm/text/README.md at main · huggingface/smollm · GitHub", "url": "https://github.com/huggingface/smollm/blob/main/text/README.md"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "huggingface.co", "ref_id": "turn22search1", "snippet": "By default, Qwen3 has thinking capabilities enabled, similar to QwQ-32B. ... def __init__(self, model_name=\"Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B\"): ... However, using a higher value may occasionally result in language", "title": "Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B · Hugging Face", "url": "https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B?local-app=docker-model-runner"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "huggingface.co", "ref_id": "turn22search2", "snippet": "Model card Files xet Community 1 ... model, tokenizer = load(\"Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B-MLX-bf16\") ... openclaw agent --local --agent main --message \"Hello from Hugging Face\" ... Qwen3 is", "title": "Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B-MLX-bf16 · Hugging Face", "url": "https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B-MLX-bf16?inference_provider=featherless-ai"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "huggingface.co", "ref_id": "turn22search3", "snippet": "Qwen3 is the latest generation of large language models in Qwen series, offering a comprehensive suite of dense and mixture-of-experts (MoE) models. ... * Uniquely", "title": "Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B · Hugging Face", "url": "https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B?local-app=vllm"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "huggingface.co", "ref_id": "turn22search4", "snippet": "Model card Files xet Community 43 ... docker model run hf.co/Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B ... -v ~/.cache/huggingface:/root/.cache/huggingface \\", "title": "Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B · Hugging Face", "url": "https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B?chat_template=default"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "api-inference.huggingface.co", "ref_id": "turn22search5", "snippet": "docker model run hf.co/mradermacher/SmolLM2-360M-Instruct-GGUF:Q4_K_M ... See https://huggingface.co/mradermacher/model_requests for some answers to questions you might have and/or if you want some ot", "title": "mradermacher/SmolLM2-360M-Instruct-GGUF · Hugging Face", "url": "https://api-inference.huggingface.co/mradermacher/SmolLM2-360M-Instruct-GGUF"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "graysoft.dev", "ref_id": "turn22search6", "snippet": "\"readme_markdown\": \"---\\nlibrary_name: transformers\\nlicense: apache-2.0\\nlanguage:\\n- en\\ntags:\\n- llama-cpp\\n- gguf-my-repo\\nbase_model: HuggingFaceTB/SmolLM2-360M-Instruct\\n---\\n\\n# ngxson/SmolLM2-", "title": "huggingfacetb/smollm2-360m-instruct-gguf - Free GGUF Download | GraySoft", "url": "https://graysoft.dev/models/hug/huggingfacetb-smollm2-360m-instruct-gguf.html"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "huggingface.co", "ref_id": "turn22search7", "snippet": "pipe = pipeline(\"text-generation\", model=\"HuggingFaceTB/SmolLM2-360M-Instruct\") ... SmolLM2 is a family of compact language models available in three size: 135M, 360M, and 1.7B parameters. ... You can", "title": "HuggingFaceTB/SmolLM2-360M-Instruct · Hugging Face", "url": "https://huggingface.co/HuggingFaceTB/SmolLM2-360M-Instruct?local-app=sglang"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "huggingface.co", "ref_id": "turn22search8", "snippet": "## Model tree for Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B ... Qwen/Qwen3-Demo 🟩 embedl/hfviewer 🌍 k2-fsa/OmniVoice 💥 pliny-the-prompter/obliteratus 📝 HuggingFaceFW/finephrase 🏆 Intel/low_bit_open_llm_leaderboard ⚡ VIDraft/gl", "title": "Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B · Hugging Face", "url": "https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B?hardware=apple-m4-pro-64gb"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "huggingface.co", "ref_id": "turn22search9", "snippet": "Image Hugging Face Smol Models Research [Button: 4.17k] ... pipe = pipeline(\"text-generation\", model=\"HuggingFaceTB/SmolLM2-360M\") ... SmolLM2 is a family of compact language models available in three", "title": "HuggingFaceTB/SmolLM2-360M · Hugging Face", "url": "https://huggingface.co/HuggingFaceTB/SmolLM2-360M?library=transformers"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "api-inference.huggingface.co", "ref_id": "turn22search10", "snippet": "lmstudio-community/Qwen3-0.6B-GGUF 0.8B • Updated Mar 10 • 3.71k • 9 WithinUsAI/Qwen3-Desert.Coder.MoE-8X0.6B-GGUF 2B • Updated 6 days ago • 379 • 2 gluschenko/omnivoice-onnx Text-to-Speech • Updated", "title": "Quantized Models for Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B – Hugging Face", "url": "https://api-inference.huggingface.co/models?other=base_model%3Aquantized%3AQwen%2FQwen3-0.6B"}]}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "01a08154-4c27-7551-9cfa-e8e7d2bcf73a", "turn_id": "01a159c7-08da-7da0-beba-8f34917dec3f", "item_id": "msg_06f6aa8593d2a892016ad77ecc5c0c87d2853db4a99be66330", "rollout_ordinal": 4549, "created_at_ms": 1792507595628, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 4549, "started_at_ms": 1792507595628, "completed_at_ms": 1792507605797}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "msg_06f6aa8593d2a892016ad77ecc5c0c87d2853db4a99be66330", "text": "Sí. **Un modelo pequeño podría servir para redactar la retroalimentación con más naturalidad**, manteniendo el análisis musical que ya tenemos.\n\nLo usaría así:\n\n**Análisis actual → observaciones verificadas → modelo pequeño → explicación para el usuario.**\n\nEl modelo recibiría datos como «en esta frase la voz estuvo más grave» y los expresaría de manera clara. **No decidiría la puntuación ni analizaría directamente el audio.**\n\nProbaría primero **Qwen3-0.6B**, cuantizado para reducir memoria y con su modo de razonamiento desactivado. Es un candidato pequeño que permite ese modo de funcionamiento; habría que comprobar su calidad en español con nuestras tomas. [Ficha oficial](https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B).\n\nPara evitar repetir el problema de consumo:\n\n- Ejecutarlo solo al solicitar una explicación, nunca mientras cantas o separas voces.\n- Limitar los hilos de CPU y la longitud de respuesta.\n- Guardar las explicaciones para no generarlas repetidamente.\n- Mantener las plantillas actuales como alternativa si falla o inventa información.\n\n**Ser pequeño no garantiza consumir poca CPU mientras genera.** La prueba debería medir tiempo, memoria, uso de CPU y, sobre todo, si respeta los resultados sin inventar consejos.\n\nMi recomendación es **evaluarlo primero aparte, sin sustituir todavía las plantillas**. No necesitaríamos entrenarlo inicialmente ni volver a depender de Ollama.", "phase": "final_answer", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
